{"research_date": "2026-09-10", "pairs": [{"pair_id": "conflict_1bc1d78091311dd85dcf8796", "claim_ids": ["claim_3ff049100bbe98cd71a14d73", "claim_79899bfb5bc501811d486e18"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_3ff049100bbe98cd71a14d73", "quote": "Therefore, US customs authorities later reclassified these vehicles as transport vehicles based on their features and intended use. This reclassification led to allegations of false declarations by Ford, potentially resulting in over $1 billion in additional tariffs.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "legal_authority": "US customs authorities", "affected_product": "vehicles"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_79899bfb5bc501811d486e18", "quote": "Merritt v. Welsh, held that tariff engineering is an acceptable practice.", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "Merritt v. Welsh", "reported_policy_status": "acceptable practice"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_93751ecc3dfc7952efe76bd6", "claim_ids": ["claim_4b607639a630dfe9aab30b51", "claim_a6cdf42442a3d5377b56cda0"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_4b607639a630dfe9aab30b51", "quote": "Between 2009 and 2013, Ford imported over 160,000 Transit Connect vehicles. Before importation, Ford installed second-row seats in order to classify them as passenger cars, which carried a 2.5% tariff rate, avoiding the high tariff rate of 25% for transport vehicles.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "duty_rate": "2.5%"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_a6cdf42442a3d5377b56cda0", "quote": "As part of the settlement, Ford agreed to pay $365 million to resolve the DOJ action.", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "duty_rate": "$365 million"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_3ceac8799c018cc9865e0219", "claim_ids": ["claim_bcf32fcb59aa6b44dac6041d", "claim_cf7c8ffe65a67501fbae49de"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_bcf32fcb59aa6b44dac6041d", "quote": "Last year, Ford settled the dispute by agreeing to pay $365 million and committed to obtaining binding customs rulings for future models, while also withdrawing its lawsuit challenging the classification.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "duty_rate": "$365 million"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_cf7c8ffe65a67501fbae49de", "quote": "As background, Ford manufactured the Transit Connect vehicles in Turkey and imported them into the United States.", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "facility": "Turkey"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_89d44a54b99294cf6b7e158f", "claim_ids": ["claim_3b0c5aa321b3b624b856b937", "claim_9640e77589a6b57234a13e5f"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_3b0c5aa321b3b624b856b937", "quote": "Also in Switzerland, this distinction led to several fines and reclassifications of pick-up trucks over the past years, as besides customs duties, particularly the automobile tax plays a vital role.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_9640e77589a6b57234a13e5f", "quote": "According to the HS Committee of the World Customs Organization, pick-ups are not considered vehicles for the transport of goods due to their relatively small loading areas.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "HS Committee of the World Customs Organization"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_266a2a776ce073b760c6d67d", "claim_ids": ["claim_6855560ba5b2d7d5d210b23d", "claim_9ff0feb7f32297e1d91e037d"], "query_ids": ["q_474"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_6855560ba5b2d7d5d210b23d", "quote": "President Trump's implementation of a 40% penalty tariff on transshipped goods, effective August 7, 2025.", "url": "https://www.e2open.com/blog/navigating-the-transshipment-crisis", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "40% penalty tariff on transshipped goods", "duty_rate": "40%", "effective_date": "August 7, 2025", "reported_policy_status": "implementation"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_9ff0feb7f32297e1d91e037d", "quote": "the Trump administration has indicated that, under some of the preliminary trade agreements it has reached with several countries, U.S. imports of goods transshipped through those countries may be subject to an additional 40 percent tariff.", "url": "https://www.strtrade.com/trade-news-resources/str-trade-report/trade-report/september/cbp-identifies-red-flags-best-practices-on-transshipping", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "preliminary trade agreements", "duty_rate": "40 percent", "reported_policy_status": "indicated"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_41d1eb6ffdefae635296fc4e", "claim_ids": ["claim_08ff06926ad3fb5a2c67d8ac", "claim_e7bc12cb626624b0ec81e403"], "query_ids": ["q_475"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_08ff06926ad3fb5a2c6